WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.443
Here are the guide's
Application Gateway commands,

2
00:00:03.443 --> 00:00:05.625
from Learn's Azure C L I reference.

3
00:00:05.625 --> 00:00:10.100
Create the policy in detection mode,
with request body inspection on.

4
00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:14.080
The C L I's default rule set is
version two point one; Learn's page,

5
00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:18.139
Secure your Azure Application
Gateway, recommends the latest,

6
00:00:18.139 --> 00:00:22.900
two point two at the guide's reading,
validated in log mode before blocking.

7
00:00:22.900 --> 00:00:24.950
So name the version you've validated.

8
00:00:24.950 --> 00:00:29.097
Add the bot protection rule set, in
commercial Azure, and a rate limit

9
00:00:29.097 --> 00:00:33.762
grouped by client address on the login
path, from Learn's rate limit examples.

10
00:00:33.762 --> 00:00:37.285
Then tune: detection for at
least one full business cycle,

11
00:00:37.285 --> 00:00:41.705
two weeks by the program's default,
reading the firewall log for matches

12
00:00:41.705 --> 00:00:46.201
on legitimate traffic, and scoping
each exception to the narrowest rule.

13
00:00:46.201 --> 00:00:49.475
Then switch to prevention,
one application at a time.

14
00:00:49.475 --> 00:00:52.905
Rollback is the same command
with the mode back to detection,

15
00:00:52.905 --> 00:00:55.375
which Learn documents for false positives.

16
00:00:55.375 --> 00:01:00.170
The guide also gives the policy as
Bicep, from Azure Verified Modules.
